From: liuqin Fedora maintainers <liuqin@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8475: describe asymmetric CPU capacities and power

Source: liuqin v0.7.0 1cd8848c87 (5.18 vendor values from the stock DT)
Rationale: the four little, three big and one prime core differ in
capacity and dynamic power. Without these properties EAS and the thermal
governor treat them as equal and can place work on the wrong cluster.
No clocks, regulators or OPPs change.
Validation and rollback: tasks/upstream-refresh/RESULT.md.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi
@@ -131,6 +131,46 @@
 	compatible = "qcom,sm8475-camcc";
 };
 
+&cpu0 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <100>;
+};
+
+&cpu1 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <100>;
+};
+
+&cpu2 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <100>;
+};
+
+&cpu3 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <100>;
+};
+
+&cpu4 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <2253>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <257>;
+};
+
+&cpu5 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <2253>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <257>;
+};
+
+&cpu6 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <2253>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <257>;
+};
+
+&cpu7 {
+	capacity-dmips-mhz = <2386>;
+	dynamic-power-coefficient = <509>;
+};
+
 &dispcc {
 	compatible = "qcom,sm8475-dispcc";
 };
